    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, the reference budget for the project is €900,000 over 5 years. our pricing model indicates a target gross margin of between 25% and 35%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To estimate a target gross margin of between 25% and 35%, let's break down the costs. our know that one-off project costs account for 30% of The global budget allocated to the project, which would be €270,000 (30% of €900,000), and recurring run costs account for 70%, which is €630,000 (70% of €900,000) over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our standard daily rates and the composition of our team, our can estimate our costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without more specific details on the project requirements and the exact team composition, it's challenging to provide an exact margin projection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "That being said, assuming our can maintain our target gross margin range, our projected margin on this contract could be between €225,000 (25% of €900,000) and €315,000 (35% of €900,000)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for cost-optimisation strategies, our can propose the following: 1. **Sovereign HDS tier and sovereign European model**: our context notes that Sovereign HDS tier and sovereign European model are more cost-efficient on the recurring side than the premium high-availability tier combined with top-tier proprietary inference." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk147> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By choosing Sovereign HDS tier and sovereign European model, our can reduce our recurring costs. 2. **Efficient team composition**: By carefully selecting the project team based on the required skills and our standard daily rates, our can optimize our one-off project costs. 3. **Phased implementation**: the project is to be conducted progressively with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter, followed by generalization to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk148> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach allows for better cost control and optimization as our can adjust our strategy based on the outcomes of a pilot phase. 4. **Change management and training**: By providing efficient change management support and staff training, our can ensure that the client's staff can effectively use the solution, reducing the need for additional support and thus optimizing costs. 5. **Low carbon infrastructure**: Our context mentions the importance of low carbon infrastructure for hosting." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk149> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging such infrastructure, our not only comply with environmental constraints but also potentially reduce energy consumption and costs associated with hosting." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk150> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By implementing these strategies, our can work within the authority's budgetary capacity while maintaining our target gross margin range, thus ensuring a mutually beneficial contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk151> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must provide an intelligent assistance tool capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities, facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk152> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy can we design to meet these requirements while ensuring explainability and traceability?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk153> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements for an intelligent assistance tool that supports hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities, our company Faber IA can leverage our company Faber IA core approach of Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk154> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) involves generating answers from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus, ensuring grounding and limiting unsupported generation. we can design an AI solution that incorporates several key components: 1. **Hybrid retrieval**: Utilize a combination of lexical and semantic search to retrieve relevant information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. 2. **Template-guided drafting**: Implement template-guided drafting capabilities for discharge summaries, medical correspondence, administrative documents, and dossier syntheses to improve the quality of written outputs. 3. **Multi-document synthesis**: Enable the AI system to synthesize information from multiple documents to provide comprehensive support for clinical-administrative activities. 4. **Action and verification suggestions**: Offer suggestions for next steps based on the dossier context and applicable rules to facilitate efficient handling of dossiers. we innovation strategy will focus on iterative development, with the following steps: 1. **Corpus selection and curation**: Collaborate with the client's experts to select and curate a relevant corpus of documents that will serve as the foundation for the AI system. 2. **Retrieval tuning**: Fine-tune the retrieval mechanism to ensure accurate and relevant information is retrieved from the corpus. 3. **Prompt and template design**: Design prompts and templates tailored to specific use cases, such as discharge summaries or medical reports, to improve the quality of generated content. 4. **Evaluation loop**: Establish an evaluation loop to assess the performance of the AI system and identify areas for improvement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk155> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explainability and traceability, we will provide: 1. **Source citations**: Include source citations for retrieved passages to enable staff to access the original information. 2. **Retrieval trace**: Maintain a retrieval trace to allow for auditing and understanding of how the AI system arrived at the AI system suggestions or generated content. 3. **Every interaction logged**: Log every interaction with the AI system to facilitate a posteriori analysis and improvement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk156> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By following this approach, we can design an intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements while ensuring explainability and traceability, ultimately supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities and improving patient care." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk157> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The authority wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The authority information systems, reduce energy consumption, and rely on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk158> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure we proposed solution aligns with these sustainability goals, and what measures can we take to minimize our proposed solution environmental impact?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk159> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As a CSR & Sustainability officer at Faber IA, I can ensure that our proposed solution aligns with these sustainability goals by leveraging we existing capabilities in green hosting and digital sobriety practices." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must take the dossier context into account where available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk160> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA have partnerships with green hosting providers such as OuraneCloud, which offers sovereign European hosting with renewable energy sources, a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and heat reuse capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk161> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This can help reduce the environmental footprint of our proposed solution." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk162> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, Faber IA practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which can contribute to minimizing energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk163> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA carbon reporting capability also allows Faber IA to monitor and report on the carbon intensity of Faber IA operations, ensuring transparency and accountability in Faber IA sustainability efforts." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk164> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To further minimize the environmental impact of our proposed solution, Faber IA can explore opportunities for optimizing energy efficiency, reducing e-waste, and promoting sustainable procurement practices throughout the project lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk165> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By prioritizing sustainability and leveraging we existing capabilities in green hosting and digital sobriety, we can ensure that our proposed solution not only meets but exceeds The authority expectations for minimizing environmental impact while delivering a high-quality AI assistance solution for hospital staff." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk166> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As part of the public tender for the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB), our consortium proposes an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities. an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities will facilitate access to information, improve the quality of written outputs, and reduce processing and documentation times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk167> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve this, our will adopt a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure, which has been successfully applied in our past references, such as regional council and mutual health insurer projects. our dedicated team for this project consists of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, with additional resources available for change management and training. an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities will provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool accessible from hospital staff work environment, supporting hospital staff in clinical-administrative activities such as retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities will also assist in drafting medical and administrative documents, handling dossiers, and ensuring the continuity of care between professionals and services. our will leverage our consortium partners, including OuraneCloud for hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure and Ligeo Santé for health-IT integration, to ensure seamless integration with the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI). an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities will provide response times compatible with daily clinical use, with a target of below 2 seconds, and an availability target of 99.9%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk168> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of security and compliance, our guarantee strict adherence to GDPR regulations, including Article 9 special-category data and Article 28 processing agreements. our will implement encryption at rest using AES-256 and in transit with TLS 1.3, as well as pseudonymisation where relevant, to protect sensitive health data. our hosting options include the Sovereign HDS tier, which meets the EU-only requirement and is powered by renewable energy. our will also provide API-type interfaces for easy embedding in existing work environments and support integration with user directories using SSO protocols like SAML and OIDC." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk169> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explainability and traceability, our AI models will provide a level of transparency that can support explainability, including source citations for retrieved passages and maintenance of a retrieval trace. our will also establish an evaluation loop to assess the performance of an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities and identify areas for improvement. our pricing model indicates a target gross margin of between 25% and 35%, with estimated one-off project costs of €270,000 and recurring run costs of €630,000 over 5 years. our propose cost-optimisation strategies, including the use of Sovereign HDS tier and sovereign European models, efficient team composition, and phased implementation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No decision may be automated. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of care." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk170> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of environmental sustainability, our will leverage our existing capabilities in green hosting and digital sobriety practices to minimize the environmental footprint of an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities. our partnership with OuraneCloud offers sovereign European hosting with renewable energy sources, a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and heat reuse capabilities. an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities aligns with the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) sustainability goals and contributes to reducing energy consumption while delivering a high-quality AI assistance solution for hospital staff. our are committed to working within the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) budgetary capacity while maintaining our target gross margin range, ensuring a mutually beneficial contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk171> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In conclusion, our consortium proposes an AI assistance solution that meets the requirements of the the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) public tender, providing an intelligent tool to support hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and minimizing environmental impact. our believe an artificial intelligence (AI) assistance solution designed to support hospital staff in their daily activities will improve the efficiency of the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) staff and the quality and safety of care delivered to patients, and our look forward to the opportunity to work with the Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) on this project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must facilitate the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and an efficient resumption of handling by another professional. 4." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regulatory and legal constraints 4.1 Personal and health data protection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Context and objectives The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is a public regional hospital serving the Belval region (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff across medical, care and medico-administrative functions)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The titleholder must guarantee strict compliance with the GDPR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Health data is processed as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9) and medical confidentiality (secret médical) must be preserved." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Data must be hosted exclusively within the European Union; no transfer of data outside the European Union is authorised; sensitive data must be appropriately protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant). 4.2 Health-data hosting (HDS)." ;
